{
  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment (config_019: image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) has been completed, yielding ~21% accuracy, which is very low and provides minimal signal about which design axes matter. The biggest uncertainty is whether RNA information adds any predictive value over image alone, which is the central question of a multimodal cellular profiling study. This experiment (config_038: multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat) is the cleanest possible extension of config_019: it holds the image encoder (resnet50) and profile setting (singleprofile) constant and adds only a standard RNA encoder (scvi_n200) with simple concat fusion. This isolates the effect of adding the RNA modality. If accuracy improves substantially, RNA is informative and we can then explore encoder/aggregation/fusion choices. If it does not improve, we know the bottleneck lies elsewhere (e.g., image encoder quality, profile complexity) and should pivot. Under a tight budget, this single-variable comparison to the existing baseline is the highest-information next step."
}

